    "body": "### Problem\n\nIf the snippet does not have a placeholder, we use insert mode instead of select mode. Then, if you use `<Esc>` to try to cancel, it leaves behind highlighting.\n\nAn example of a snippet without placeholders would be this one from lua_ls\n```\nfunction $1($2)\n\t$0\nend\n```\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bcc55741-9224-4635-aad0-46a56383a09c\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```\nvim.pack.add({\n  'https://github.com/mason-org/mason.nvim',\n  'https://github.com/neovim/nvim-lspconfig',\n})\nrequire('mason').setup()\nvim.lsp.enable('lua_ls')\n\nvim.o.autocomplete = true\nvim.o.complete = \"o\"\nvim.o.completeopt = { \"menuone\", \"noinsert\", \"popup\" }\n```\n \n1. Install lua_ls and then use the above init.lua\n2. Type `func`, then go to insert the snippet with `<C-y>`\n3. Type `foo` then hit `<Esc>`\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe highlighting is cleared when you go from insert mode to normal mode.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1448+gfbc5a769aa\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nn/a, vim doesn't have LSP\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nLinux Mint 22.3\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nGhostty 1.3.1\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\nRepo build",
